	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Browse Netlify sites, deploys and settings from Alfred.

Type `nf` to list your Netlify sites with their latest deploy status.

![Netlify sites in Alfred](images/about/main.png)

## Commands

* `nf &lt;query&gt;` - filter your sites by name or domain.
* `nf &lt;site&gt; &gt;` - the site: Builds, Environment variables, Settings, Open live site, Trigger deploy.
* `nf &lt;site&gt; &gt; builds` - builds, newest first, with status and failure reason; `&gt; &lt;id&gt;` opens a build's detail.
* `nf &lt;site&gt; &gt; env` - environment variables; `nf &lt;site&gt; &gt; settings` - build and domain settings.
* Delete the last part of the path to go back; text after it filters the page.
* First row on every page is the page itself: Enter opens it in Netlify, Tab goes back.
* Enter on a site, section or build - go into it.
* Cmd+Enter on a site - open its Netlify dashboard; Alt+Enter opens the live site; Ctrl+Enter triggers a deploy.
* Cmd+Enter on a build - open its deploy preview; Ctrl+Enter cancels an active build.
* Enter on an environment variable - copy `KEY=value`; Cmd+Enter copies the value only.
* Enter on a detail or setting - copy it, or open it when it is a link.

## Setup

* Open Configure Workflow and paste a Netlify personal access token (User Settings &gt; Applications &gt; Personal access tokens).

## Maintenance

* `:nf` - cache size (Enter reveals the folder) and Empty Cache.
